        <mxCell id="t25" value="Parallel inside the lane: 2.0.3.2 and 3.0.4.2 share only the toolchain, so they ran side by side. Everything after them is sequential." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#6b6e7b;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="440" width="817" height="17" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t26" value="3.0.4.1 has no contract dependency at all — it is a toolchain subtask, so lane C could start on day one like lanes A, B and F." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#6b6e7b;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="462" width="768" height="17" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="t27" value="2.0.3.2's implementation commit was mis-tagged [5.0.8.2]: a concurrent session swept its staged files into another commit. Recorded as an anomaly, history not rewritten." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#6b6e7b;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="24" y="484" width="1030" height="17" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
